# Origin of the FastAPI backend. The client appends the API version itself
# (`/api/v1`), so this must NOT include a path.
#
# Prefer the literal 127.0.0.1 over `localhost`. `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`
# binds 127.0.0.1 only, which is IPv4, so a resolver that returns ::1 first
# makes a client try an address nothing is listening on before falling back.
#
# This is defensive, not a fix for anything observed here: Chrome was measured
# against both spellings and behaved identically. The two-second stall that
# looked like a front-end problem was on a different hop entirely - the
# application's own connection to PostgreSQL. See DATABASE_URL in the
# project-root .env.example.
#
# Leave it empty for a same-origin deployment where the API serves the SPA;
# requests then go to a relative `/api/v1/...`.
#
# The backend must list this app's origin in CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (it defaults
# to http://localhost:5173, which is the Vite dev server). That is the origin
# the browser reports for the front end, and it is unaffected by the address
# used for the API.
#
# Nothing secret belongs in this file: every VITE_* variable is inlined into the
# JavaScript bundle and is therefore public.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
